{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"algebraicConnectivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traps when the work limit is spent: 4,000 + 20√n products on σI − L (then shift-invert),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000 shift-invert products, 20,000 + 2n per solve. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached it in the measurements."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At least two vertices, and "},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/algebraicconnectivity(normalized:tolerance:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The algebraic connectivity λ₂: the second smallest eigenvalue of the Laplacian L (of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalized Laplacian N with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":"), 0 exactly when the graph is not connected (a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight-0 edge does not connect). NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraic_connectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; Fiedler 1973."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21algebraicConnectivity10norm